.title 15 dB finger-loaded coupler on JLC RO4350B 0.508 mm (5 GHz), velocity-equalised (#41)
# The coupled section carries interdigital fingers on each line's inner edge (worked example 14). comb-over has
# no model of its own for them: the section's even/odd impedances and effective permittivities on the fingers
# line come from an openEMS extraction (tools/fingerdesign.mjs: εe, εo de-embedded from 8- and 14-cell sections,
# Ze, Zo fitted with those held). They hold for this substrate and these dimensions only. The loss Q is the
# backbones'. In openEMS this coupler has 22.8 dB directivity at 5 GHz (the plain 15 dB coupler: 9.1 dB);
# comb-over's own figure (32 dB) is an upper bound, as its layout's corners and arm coupling are not modelled.
.freq 1G 9G 801
.ref 5G
.substrate jlc-ro4350b-0.508
port in    # 1
port thru  # 2
port cpl   # 3
port iso   # 4
cline K geom=msl W=0.9463mm S=0.4749mm      # the backbones
  fingers wf=0.13mm lf=0.3692mm p=1.065mm Ze=59.81 Zo=41.75 ee=3.095 eo=3.092
  len 8.52mm                                # 8 whole cells: λ/4 at 5 GHz
  A in   cpl
  B thru iso
end
.plot ylim=-60,0 db(S11) db(S21) db(S31) db(S41)
.plot title=Directivity_(dB) db(S31/S41)
.layout coupler K
